WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.063
A pilot isn't a deployment.

3
00:00:03.063 --> 00:00:07.581
In this module the pilot becomes a
migration: users move ring by ring,

4
00:00:07.581 --> 00:00:12.423
each ring exits on criteria you measure,
the V P N route for an application

5
00:00:12.423 --> 00:00:17.587
goes only after its wave holds, and anything
can be rolled back in a known order.

6
00:00:17.587 --> 00:00:22.319
Then each network finding gets an
evidence package an assessor can check:

7
00:00:22.319 --> 00:00:26.974
configuration, test, operational,
exception, and reassessment evidence.

8
00:00:26.974 --> 00:00:30.014
The assessor recommends a
finding ready for closure,

9
00:00:30.014 --> 00:00:32.225
and the authorizing official decides.

10
00:00:32.225 --> 00:00:35.476
In the lab, you rehearse the
rollback on your test tenant,

11
00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:39.000
and keep the exports that show
the state before and after it.
